 II, discoveries by the Allies, and the extraordinary tasks of preserving, tracking, and returning by the American Monuments officers and their colleagues. Nicholas was awarded the Légion d'Honneur by France. Despite the regular accounts of impending destruction of art works, Nicholas also recounts a veneration for art on the part of people of all sides of the conflict, and what amounts to desperate and sometimes heroic activity. The villains, unsurprisingly, are often the Nazis, particularly Adolf Hitler and Hermann Göring; the activities of Western art dealers are often questionable, as well.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rape_of_Europa_(book)","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"The Rape of Europa","author":"Lynn H. Nicholas","publisher":"Knopf","publicationDate":"1994","publicationPlace":"United States","pages":"498","isbn":"0-679-40069-9 |isbn_note= (Knopf edition), 0-679-75686-8 (Vintage Edition)","language":"English","subject":"Art theft, World War II in Europe, art conservation"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-the-rape-of-europa-the-fate-of-europe-s-treasures-in-the-third-reich-and-the-second-world-war-ly"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-nbcc-nonfiction-wikipedia-national-book-critics-circle-award-for-nonfiction","label":"Wikipedia: National Book Critics Circle Award for Nonfiction","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Book_Critics_Circle_Award_for_Nonfiction","accessedAt":"2026-07-23T19:41:30.257Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.bookcritics.org/awards/"},{"id":"source-open-library-the-rape-of-europa-the-fate-of-europe-s-treasures-in-the-third-reich-and-the-second-world-war-ly","label":"Open Library metadata for The Rape of Europa: The Fate of Europe's Treasures in the Third Reich and the Second World War",